+Use case: ui-mockup
+Create one finished original illustrated game art direction mockup, D1 "Carrière à l'heure dorée", for Crownforge's BOOMTOOTH. Output exactly 1536 × 1024 pixels, landscape 3:2, opaque background.
+STYLE: adult Franco-Belgian comic / 2D cartoon. Bold slightly irregular black brush outlines 4–7 px at 1536 width, thinner interior lines, simple instantly legible silhouettes. Strict two-tone cel shading plus a sharp off-white highlight per volume. Controlled saturated colors. Draw wood grain, chipped stone, hammered metal and plaid with hatching and ink marks. No photorealism, smooth 3D, plastic, airbrush, soft shadows, gradients, generic neon, bloom, bokeh, border effects, emojis or system fonts. Original designs, no imitation of another brand.
+SCENE: Northern pine valley in late afternoon, strong low orange sunlight from left, crisp rim light. Background gray-blue granite mountain half carved into a gigantic beaver head, clearly visible above the grid, timber scaffolding, ropes and pulleys. Midground dark pine forest, river and large log dam with a small waterfall. Foreground crates, cut logs and wood chips. Palette burnt orange #E8742A, pine green #2F5D46, granite #6F7F92, TNT red #D7332B, gold #F2B233, cream #F4E6C8, ink #1B1410.
+COMPOSITION: dominant square 5-column × 5-row slot grid in central-left area, approximately x=320–990 y=215–885, all 25 equal square cells visible, frontal and undistorted. Frame of squared wooden beams bolted with steel fittings and rivets, worn yellow-black caution stripes at corners. Each cell darker than scenery. Large distinct symbols filling 85–95 percent of their cells, heavy ink outlines. The illustrated wooden carved game logo "BOOMTOOTH" sits above the upper-left of grid, with a small fuse and spark, clearly readable, no overlap obscuring grid. Leave scenic mountain above and river/dam visible to left. Buck stands fully visible to right of grid, ground contact shadow, no overlap hiding cells. Compact HUD along bottom, all elements inside image. Maintain safe margins for logo, mascot and controls.
+GRID CONTENT: exactly these 25 symbols, organized row by row, with repetition only of the same families:
+row 1: yellow hardhat; blue-handled pickaxe; raccoon demolitions expert bust; green lantern; purple metal canteen.
+row 2: muscular moose bust with large antlers; golden dynamite crate stamped "WILD"; otter surveyor bust holding rolled blueprint and pencil behind ear; woodpecker driller bust wearing hardhat and holding drill bit; single red dynamite stick with short fuse and NO text.
+row 3: green lantern; raccoon bust; red dynamite bundle with detonator labeled "SCATTER"; yellow hardhat; moose bust.
+row 4: purple canteen; woodpecker bust; blue-handled pickaxe; otter bust; golden dynamite crate stamped "WILD".
+row 5: single red dynamite stick with short fuse and NO text; moose bust; green lantern; raccoon bust; purple canteen.
+The raccoon has its natural black face mask, welding goggles and a sly smile. All four animal bust families must look expressive and distinct. Each cell contains just its specified symbol.
+MASCOT: Buck Boomtooth, a vain daredevil construction foreman, short stocky muscular beaver with reddish-brown fur and a clearly visible large flat scaly paddle tail. Exactly two front incisors, his own LEFT front incisor is GOLD (viewer-right tooth), other tooth cream. Dented orange hardhat with headlamp, rolled-sleeve red-and-black plaid lumberjack shirt, suspenders, tool belt, match in corner of mouth. Raised eyebrows, mischievous broad grin displaying gold tooth. Proud stance, one boot on a crate and other on ground; one hand rests on the handle of a wooden plunger detonator; other hand holds a red dynamite stick with lit fuse. Both hands distinct and anatomically coherent. Whole character, tail, hat, feet and dynamite visible.
+HUD: illustrated "BUY BONUS" button bottom left; then exactly three blank value plaques for balance, bet and win, without letters or numbers. Bet plaque flanked by minus and plus graphical controls. Large round illustrated "SPIN" button bottom right. A few small circular icon-only buttons. Handmade organic wood/metal forms, no rectangular dashboard styling.
+TEXT: only exact words "BOOMTOOTH", "BUY BONUS", "SPIN", "WILD", "SCATTER". No other text, no numbers, no studio name, no labels, signature or watermark. Output a complete production-quality art direction image, not a sketch or explanatory presentation.
+CORRECTION FOR FINAL PASS: Use the supplied image as the edit target. Preserve its exact composition, all 25 symbols and their positions, all correct lettering, Buck's pose, left gold incisor, visible tail, dam and carved mountain. Change only the rendering style: substantially simplify into bold flat 2D comic shapes with exactly two flat tones per material and a single sharp cream highlight. Remove painterly microtexture, realistic fur strands, realistic rock/water texture, all smooth shading and gradients, and lantern glow. Use thick slightly irregular brush outlines and sparse deliberate drawn hatching only. Sky in flat graphic color bands and stylized cloud shapes; water in clean flat shapes; fur as simple clumps. No photorealistic detail. Preserve readable handmade text verbatim, and keep complete image at exactly 1536 × 1024 with an opaque background.

